------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY SCOPE  (Honesty #2 No-scope-narrowing)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web <ReleaseNotes> reads a COMPILE-TIME-STATIC generated module (`@/generated/changelog` CHANGELOG)
and calls only useTranslation. There is NO fetch, NO React-Query cache, NO Promise -> therefore NO loading
/ error / stale / offline branch (there is nothing to fetch, fail, age, or disconnect from). Reproducing
those generic states would FABRICATE behaviour the source does not have, so this surface reproduces only
the source's REAL branches — exactly the disposition the accepted sibling presentational surfaces Accordion
(0203), Delta (0081), MetricCard (0095), InlineCallout (0124), and ActiveFilterChips (0147) used. The REAL
branches, all reproduced + tested:
  • populated list      : newest `limit` releases (web CHANGELOG.slice(0, limit)), one card open.
  • collapsed card       : header only (gift glyph + v{version} + badge chip + date + chevron at 0°).
  • expanded card        : header + body ("What's New" heading + change list), chevron at 180°, top border.
  • single-open accordion: opening one release collapses any other (web expanded === version; setExpanded
                           (isExpanded ? null : version)); first release open on appear (releases[0]?.version).
  • per-change dot tint   : added/changed/fixed/removed/deprecated/security (web DOT_TINT), via status tokens.
  • badge classification  : latest/stable/beta (web BADGE_VARIANT + ICON_TINT + BADGE_KEY label).
  • empty-changes leaf    : the native never-a-blank-box peer of an expanded release with no changes.
  • empty list            : limit<=0 / empty changelog -> friendly ReleaseNotesEmptyState (web renders nothing).
  • reduced motion        : open/close + chevron animate via easeInOut(normal); nil (instant) under reduce.
Data source  : the static generated changelog (web @/generated/changelog). Native ships a faithful built-in
               snapshot (ReleaseNotes.Data) AND accepts host-injected entries via ReleaseNotes(entries:) —
               the native peer of the web static import. No HTTP from the view (P1/S8).
Shared comps : none mapped (the web GlassPanel + Badge chrome is reproduced inline with design tokens; the
               prompt lists no shared-component dependency and allowed-files = ReleaseNotes.* only).
Charts/maps  : none (the web source uses none) -> Swift Charts / MapKit not required.
i18n keys    : web t() keys mirrored 1:1 (changelog.badges.latest/stable/beta, changelog.releaseNotes.heading
               "What's New"); native a11y additions resolved through the same P1/S10 facade. No English
               literals in the Swift views (all via the facade / verbatim caller data).
Telemetry    : view.opened emitted once with slug "ReleaseNotes" (P1/S11).
a11y         : each release header is one tap target with explicit label (v{version}, badge, date) + value
               (Expanded/Collapsed, the spoken peer of aria-expanded) + hint (Show/Hide release notes);
               chevron + dots hidden from VoiceOver; each change row folds its category label + text into one
               phrase so the color-coded dot meaning is announced; reduce-motion honored; Dynamic Type via
               tokens; empty leaves are single combined, labelled elements.

